; bale-crier credit timer — user-level. See bale-crier-credit.service for the install notes.
;
; This timer, not the service, is the unit to enable:
;   systemctl --user enable --now bale-crier-credit.timer
;
; Hourly, with a two-minute spread rather than bale-crier.timer's ten: an hourly check has
; less room to spread into. The latch, not the check, is what keeps a repeated look from
; becoming a repeated message, so checking often costs nothing.
;
; bale-crier.timer does not run the credit watcher — it owns this timer — so the
; two timers cannot race over one latch.

[Unit]
Description=Check the AvalAI credit hourly

[Timer]
OnCalendar=hourly
Persistent=true
RandomizedDelaySec=2m

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
